From 2018d1df352f6d4303e9e086f08c767202ef2192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:19:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gx: paper edges, distance-field text and shadow draws

aurora/paper.h, the application's draw-only paper effects, each through the
GX command stream (GX_AURORA_SET_PAPER) so it lands between the draws around
it:
- aurora_set_paper_edges: an alpha-tested cut-out (GX_GREATER / GX_GEQUAL
  against a real threshold) gets an edge one pixel wide: alpha to coverage
  with MSAA when it doesn't blend, else faded into its source-alpha blend.
- aurora_set_paper_distance_field: the texture at that data address holds a
  distance field; each stage sampling it thresholds it per pixel (fwidth),
  sharp at any scale.
- aurora_set_paper_shadow: while on, each draw is a translucent dark copy of
  its own alpha, blended, depth written with GX_LESS (overlaps darken once),
  culling nothing.
In ShaderConfig's spare bits (edgeAA, shadowFill, sdfMaps), so the pipeline
cache keeps them apart; off, every draw is as before. Hooks kept apart from
the earlier patches' lines, so each of them still checks as applied.
---
